PKG=va200030
NAME=va2000-k30 1.1.0-3 - MNT VA2000 graphics card module (/dev/va2000), k30 line
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.1.0-3
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none va2000
VENDOR=amix
PSTAMP=amix-va200030-1.1.0-3
APKG_KBOOTSET=1.1.0.261115-46
# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2, C3-5 sec 1): a role=module entry of the #ext
# kpkg block (line=k30, kabi=k30.1.2), never an ordinary entry.  Catalog
# name va2000-k30, pkginst va200030; VERSION is the package's 1.1.0-3, the
# module's 1.1.0-1 (the fork's module/VERSION at
# kernel/drivers/va2000/va2000.pin).  The device node is in class va2000
# (C3-5 v18 sec 1.2).  APKG_KBOOTSET is the module's
# kbootset floor (C2-2 v7): kbootset -46, whose registry has major c 68;
# the catalog row carries it as kbootset=, and apkg installs that first.
APKG_DESC=MNT VA2000 RTG graphics card (/dev/va2000: its registers and framebuffer for programs such as the X server Xrtg), Antti Sokero's driver (MIT) as a demand-class kernel module for the 68030 module kernel kernel-k30-m; needs kbootset 1.1.0.261115-46 or later, which apkg installs first; tested in emulation only (no board present): /etc/conf/mod.d/va2000, /dev/va2000, /usr/include/va2000.h, the page va2000(7) and the card file /etc/display.d/va2000, with which xstart starts X on the card (Xrtg -card va2000, x11r63 6.3-10 or later).
DESC=The MNT VA2000 RTG graphics card: Antti Sokero's va2000-amix driver (MIT), from our fork, built as an amix-dlm kernel module for the 68030 line (kabi k30.1.2, so it loads on the 1.1 kernels).  Programs such as the X server Xrtg open /dev/va2000, set a display mode with ioctl, draw into the framebuffer through mmap and switch the monitor between the Amiga's picture and the card's.  The console stays on the Amiga's own display: a module cannot carry the static driver's console changes.  Demand class: loaded at the first open of /dev/va2000 and kept only when it finds a board (AutoConfig 0x6D6E:0x01, firmware 5 or later); character major 68, its node /dev/va2000 (c 68 0, 0660 root sys: root and the group sys may open it, as it maps the card's registers) shipped by the package; never unloaded.  On the 68030 the framebuffer has the default class, the only one there.  It needs kbootset 1.1.0.261115-46 or later, whose registry has major 68; apkg installs it first.  /usr/include/va2000.h is the driver's interface for programs; the page is va2000(7).  /etc/display.d/va2000 is the card's file for xstart (display.d(4)): with card auto, or card va2000 in /etc/display, xstart runs the X server Xrtg -card va2000 (x11r63 6.3-10 or later) on the card; with no board the node does not open and xstart takes the next card.  No parameters; /etc/conf/modreg.d/va2000 holds the package's defaults (none).  The package writes no boot store; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).  Run on a real card on the 68040/68060 line (va2000-k46); this 68030 package not yet on a real card.  In emulation, where no VA2000 can be fitted: the install and a boot with the module in the set.  MIT.
